Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: refresh BA inactivity for NPU TX

NPU forwarding bypasses the mac80211 transmit paths that update the TX
aggregation last_tx timestamp. The TX-status refresh currently covers WED
only. A peer-negotiated nonzero BA timeout can therefore expire even while
NPU-offloaded traffic continues to produce accepted TX status reports.

Refresh the aggregation session for NPU as well as WED, retaining the
station guard and existing TID extraction. This does not change timeout
negotiation or keep a session alive without TX status activity.

---
--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -1604,7 +1604,8 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (mtk_wed_device_active(&dev->mt76.mmio.wed) && wcid->sta) {
+	if ((mtk_wed_device_active(&dev->mt76.mmio.wed) ||
+	     mt76_npu_device_active(mdev)) && wcid->sta) {
 		struct ieee80211_sta *sta;
 		u8 tid;
 
